※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 3210 LANG_ATTR_UNKNOWN_ABI

※ A convention is a name the target has to know, since where the arguments go
※ is the target's to say.  One nothing knows quietly meant the language's own
※ convention under a name nothing would mangle, which is two surprises at once:
※ a program that links only by luck, and one whose calls follow rules the other
※ side never agreed to.

@[abi("stdcall")]
fn elsewhere(n: u64) → u64:
    n + 1u64

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
